    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 109\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 405, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to adding certain proper-\n      ties to the definition  of  a  qualified  historic  home  for  the\n      historic homeownership rehabilitation credit\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would  expand,  for purposes of the historic homeownership\nrehabilitation tax credit, the definition of a \"qualified historic home\"\nto include historic homes located in New  York  City  in  a  \"qualifying\ncensus  tract\"  as  of  January  1, 2017, provided the historic home was\nowned by the taxpayer on January 1, 2010.\n \n  The existing historic homeownership rehabilitation tax credit has been\navailable since 2007 to homeowners rehabilitating their homes throughout\nNew York State. The expanded eligibility criteria  of  this  bill  would\npermit the tax credit for a historic home that was owned by the taxpayer\nbut  presumably  is no longer and located in area that previously quali-\nfied as a low-income  community  but  presumably  no  longer  does.  The\nrationale  for expanding this credit and the universe of homeowners whom\nwould be able to claim the credit is  not  clear,  but  the  State  does\nanticipate  a  fiscal  impact;  as  a  result,  this  concept  should be\ndiscussed in the context of the budget.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
